  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "Vent piping attached to the bonnet of RRC-V-67B was not designed to prevent high cycle fatigue. This resulted in cyclic fatigue of a weld on a 3/4-inch vent line from the RRC-V-67B socket welded connection. This is a legacy issue associated with the original design's lack of dynamic analysis, or with the 1996 and 1997 GE analysis and testing of small-bore piping in support of Adjustable Speed Drive modifications.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "design deficiency - high cycle fatigue of small-bore vent piping weld",
    "provisional": true
  },
